max number of lines met by 7 busy cells: 44 (e.g. [(0, 0, 0), (0, 0, 5), (1, 4, 1), (2, 3, 3), (3, 2, 2), (4, 1, 4), (5, 5, 0)])
a non-busy cell lies on at most 4 lines, so a 7-set with a non-busy cell meets at most 46 lines
=> the bound 46 of the proof holds (it is not attained by busy sets: the maximum there is 44); 46 < 47 is all that is used
